  "published": "2026-06-26T02:12:29.437Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Architectural Optimization: Shifted from Task-based Async/Await to a high-performance Event-Driven Sync model to minimize State Machine overhead and eliminate GC pressure during massive request handling.\n      - Resource Reallocation: Adjusted Worker Pool ratios to 90% Sync Workers / 10% Async Workers. Reduced Async Worker queue capacity from 1/4 to 1/10 to reflect the reduced reliance on asynchronous task scheduling.\n      - Performance Tuning: Applied [MethodImpl(MethodImplOptions.AggressiveInlining)] across hot paths to reduce call stack overhead and improve instruction cache locality.\n      - Documentation: Added comprehensive inline XML documentation for core components to enhance maintainability and developer experience.\n      - Stability Improvements: Refined worker distribution to better align with the zero-allocation Buffer-Model, significantly reducing RAM footprint and memory fragmentation under high throughput.",
